# Trend Regime & Swing Structure
#
# A worked example exercising every primitive in the grammar together:
# an EMA trend filter, ATR-based volatility bands (Wilder-smoothed via
# prev(), the same technique rsi() uses internally), an RSI veto, swing-
# high/low tracking via held() (arbitrary-duration state, not a fixed
# lookback), a daily-timeframe trend confirmation via series() (multi-
# timeframe read of the SAME instrument, via symbol.ticker()), a
# session-aware entry condition, and five different visual output types.

input fast_len   = int(20, min=5, max=100)
input slow_len   = int(50, min=10, max=300)
input atr_len    = int(14, min=5, max=50)
input atr_mult   = float(3.0, min=1.0, max=6.0)
input rsi_len    = int(14, min=5, max=50)
input band_color = color("#2196F3")

# --- trend filter ---
fast_ema = ema(close, input.fast_len)
slow_ema = ema(close, input.slow_len)
uptrend  = fast_ema > slow_ema

# --- ATR volatility bands, Wilder-smoothed (prev() = this formula's own
#     previous value — the same recursive technique rsi() uses internally) ---
atr_raw    = prev(1) * (input.atr_len - 1) / input.atr_len + true_range() / input.atr_len
upper_band = fast_ema + input.atr_mult * atr_raw
lower_band = fast_ema - input.atr_mult * atr_raw

# --- swing structure: held() persists a value for however many bars it
#     takes until the next swing forms — not a fixed n-bar lookback ---
is_new_swing_high = high > highest(ref(high, 1), 10)
is_new_swing_low  = low < lowest(ref(low, 1), 10)
swing_high = held(is_new_swing_high, high)
swing_low  = held(is_new_swing_low, low)

# --- momentum veto and higher-timeframe confirmation ---
rsi_ok_long    = rsi(close, input.rsi_len) < 70
daily_trend_up = close > sma(series(symbol.ticker(), "1d", "close"), 20)

# --- the actual entry condition, combining all of the above ---
entry_long = uptrend and rsi_ok_long and daily_trend_up and close > swing_high and session.is_open()

# --- outputs: two lines filled between, a band, a marker, a background ---
fast_line    = line(fast_ema)
slow_line    = line(slow_ema)
band_out     = band(upper_band, lower_band, color=input.band_color)
entry_marker = marker(entry_long, "triangle-up", "green")
regime_bg    = background(uptrend, "#e8f5e9")
trend_fill   = fill(fast_line, slow_line, "#90caf9")
